🧮 Dynamic Programming Pattern Sheet (10 Core Templates)
🟩 1️⃣ Fibonacci / Simple Recurrence

Concept:
Each state depends on a fixed number of previous states.

Recurrence:

dp[i] = dp[i-1] + dp[i-2]


Examples:

Climbing Stairs

Fibonacci Number

Decode Ways

Complexity:

Time: O(n)

Space: O(1) (by storing last 2 states)

🟩 2️⃣ 1D DP — Pick / Not Pick (House Robber Type)

Concept:
At each index, choose to take or skip an element.

Recurrence:

dp[i] = max(nums[i] + dp[i-2], dp[i-1])


Examples:

House Robber I & II

Delete and Earn

Max Sum of Non-Adjacent Elements

Complexity: O(n)

🟩 3️⃣ 2D Grid DP (Paths / Min Cost)

Concept:
You move in grid — right or down; each cell depends on top and left.

Recurrence:

dp[i][j] = grid[i][j] + min(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])


Examples:

Minimum Path Sum

Unique Paths

Dungeon Game

Complexity: O(m×n)

🟩 4️⃣ Subset Sum / Knapsack Pattern

Concept:
At each element, you either include or exclude it.

Recurrence:

dp[i][target] = dp[i-1][target] || dp[i-1][target - nums[i]]


Examples:

Subset Sum

Partition Equal Subset Sum

0/1 Knapsack

Complexity: O(n×sum)

🟩 5️⃣ Coin Change / Unbounded Knapsack

Concept:
You can reuse elements (coins) multiple times.

Recurrence:

dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[i - coin] + 1)


(For combinations, use nested loops in correct order)

Examples:

Coin Change I & II

Minimum Coins to Make Amount

Complexity: O(n×amount)

🟩 6️⃣ Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS)

Concept:
Find max increasing chain.

Recurrence:

dp[i] = 1 + max(dp[j]) where nums[i] > nums[j]


Examples:

LIS

Russian Doll Envelopes

Longest Chain of Pairs

Complexity: O(n²) or O(n log n)

🟩 7️⃣ String Matching (LCS / Edit Distance)

Concept:
Compare two strings character by character.

Recurrence (LCS):

if s1[i] == s2[j]:
  dp[i][j] = 1 + dp[i-1][j-1]
else:
  dp[i][j] = max(dp[i-1][j], dp[i][j-1])


Examples:

Longest Common Subsequence

Edit Distance

Minimum Deletions/Insertions

Complexity: O(m×n)

🟩 8️⃣ Partition DP / Interval DP

Concept:
Split a sequence into parts; try all partition points.

Recurrence:

dp[i][j] = min(dp[i][k] + dp[k+1][j] + cost)


Examples:

Matrix Chain Multiplication

Burst Balloons

Palindrome Partitioning II

Complexity: O(n³)

🟩 9️⃣ DP on Subsequences

Concept:
For each element → either include it in the subsequence or not.

Recurrence:

dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j] + dp[i-1][j - nums[i]]


Examples:

Count Subsets with Sum K

Target Sum

Number of Subsequences with Given Difference

Complexity: O(n×sum)

🟩 🔟 Bitmask DP / State Compression

Concept:
Used when you have small n (≤20) and want to track used states via bitmask.

Recurrence:

dp[mask] = min(dp[mask], dp[mask ^ (1 << j)] + cost)


Examples:

Traveling Salesman Problem (TSP)

Assign Jobs / Match Tasks

Minimum XOR Sum of Two Arrays

Complexity: O(n² × 2ⁿ)

